   "evidence": "`Classification.lean:187-191, 268-272, 360-364` add only `_apply`. In-repo precedent for a classification equiv characterizes both directions: `TauCeti/GroupTheory/TriangleGroup/Regular.lean:214` `coe_regularIsoClassEquiv_symm_apply` together with `Regular.lean:223` `coe_regularIsoClassEquiv_mk`, with the docstring at `Regular.lean:204-206` naming both as the characterization.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicTopology/ThricePuncturedSphere/Classification.lean",
   "fix": "Add the three inverse-direction lemmas as `@[simp]`, each next to its `_apply`: `(tripleEquiv.symm t).triple = t`, `(ConnectedCoverClass.isoClassEquiv.symm c).isoClass = c`, `(ConnectedPointedCoverClass.markedClassEquiv.symm c).markedClass = c` (proof: `rw [\u2190 tripleEquiv_apply, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]` and analogues). This restores simp confluence with the `_apply` lemmas and gives downstream the realisation statement through the equiv.",
   "issue": "`tripleEquiv` (line 182), `ConnectedCoverClass.isoClassEquiv` (264) and `ConnectedPointedCoverClass.markedClassEquiv` (355) each get only the forward `@[simp] _apply` lemma (191, 269, 361). The inverse \u2014 the realisation direction, which is the point of the surjectivity half \u2014 has no characteristic lemma, and because `tripleEquiv C = C.triple` is `@[simp]`, `Equiv.apply_symm_apply`/`symm_apply_apply` can no longer fire on these equivs: a goal `(tripleEquiv.symm t).triple = t` matches neither `tripleEquiv ?C` nor `tripleEquiv (tripleEquiv.symm ?x)`, so `simp` cannot close it and a consumer must hand-rewrite `\u2190 tripleEquiv_apply` before `Equiv.apply_symm_apply`. Same for `(isoClassEquiv.symm c).isoClass = c` and `(markedClassEquiv.symm c).markedClass = c`.",
   "line": "191"
  }
 ],
